        <p class="review-author">V&A Museum</p>
        <p class="review-excerpt">The great pleasure of this exhibition is its insistence on holding both sides of Morris together: the luxury wallpapers and the revolutionary politics, the exquisite handcraft and the rage at industrial capitalism. He is richer, and stranger, than either camp usually acknowledges.</p>
